**Why this matters:** Modern WAFs (like WAFs from Cloudflare, Cloudflare WAF, or similar) don't parse SQL queries literally. They parse them byte-for-byte, so `$1` literally becomes `(` plus the rest of the query, which looks like a string that won't match any known SQL fragment.

